    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm having a nightmare with our jenkins pipeline. the unit test stage is being super flaky. it fails about 20% of the time but the codebase hasn't changed and the tests pass if i just retry the build. i've checked the basic stuff but i can't figure out what's causing these non-deterministic failures. any ideas on how to isolate the environment or what might be causing this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Flaky tests, especially when they're intermittent, are a nightmare! It's often related to environmental instability, like a rogue dependency or a race condition. Try to run your unit tests in a completely isolated environment, perhaps a fresh Docker container, to see if the flakiness persists. If the issue disappears in the clean environment, then the problem is likely something specific to your Jenkins agent setup, like shared state or resource contention.",
      "source": "target",
