    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, i'll look into the thread timing... but everything looks so clean. it's honestly starting to feel like there's some kind of glitch in the system because the logs don't show any obvious errors before the crash, it just... stops. like something is messing with the process mid-run. do you think it could be something like memory leaks or just weird network jitter?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A silent failure mid-run, with no clear log message, is deeply frustrating. It sounds like you might be facing a subtle resource exhaustion issue, which can be a slow, creeping memory leak, or perhaps a transient network hiccup that causes a process to hang and time out unexpectedly. If you suspect memory, try running the test suite under a memory profiler or limit the memory available to the container to see if the failures become more consistent when the system is under more stress.\n\nIt's also worth checking if any of your tests interact with external services—even if they're mocked, sometimes the mocking framework itself can introduce subtle timing dependencies. If you have any external dependencies, even if they are just internal services, try to mock them *more* aggressively to eliminate network jitter as a variable.",
      "source": "target",
